Version: 1.0.1 (Patch Release)

Overview
--------
This patch introduces the footer feature for OpenClaw Telegram integration.
The footer is displayed in private-chat replies to provide additional context
and attribution information.

Key Features
------------
- Adds configurable footer text to Telegram message responses
- Maintains backward compatibility with existing integrations
- Supports dynamic footer content based on conversation context

Deployment Flow
---------------
This patch follows a safe deployment procedure:

1. DRY-RUN: Execute the patch in dry-run mode first to verify all changes
   without making actual modifications to the live environment.

2. BACKUP: Create a complete backup of current configuration and code
   before applying any changes.

3. ROLLBACK: If any issues are detected, use the rollback procedure to
   restore the previous stable version immediately.

4. RESTART: After successful deployment, restart the Telegram service
   to apply all changes and verify the footer displays correctly.

Technical Details
-----------------
- File changes: Minimal modifications to the response handler module
- No database migrations required
- Configuration can be updated via environment variables

